From 8fa1f96bfe35ea56ca64e09a38f976e757bfd2e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ramya Gnanasekar <quic_rgnanase@quicinc.com>
Date: Fri, 15 Nov 2024 23:42:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:CP:wifi:ath12k: Add peer delete all support WMI cmd

In current flow, when interface is brought down, peer delete will be
sent to firmware for each client and peer delete response will be received for
each client. There are below concern in doing so:
        * This may cause ring backpressure when max clients(512) is
connected.
        * Also for each peer delete, driver will wait for peer unmap
event and peer delete response thus causing a delay the vdev down.

To optimize this, before sending vdev stop, peer delete all will be sent
for the corresponding vdev. Upon receiving this, firmware will send peer
unmap for each client and one peer delete all response.

Sequence for MLO client is below:
	* Individual peer delete for the partner peers
	* Peer delete all for the link which is going down

Firmware will send peer delete all response event with status. When
status is failure, driver will do self cleanup of peers except self BSS
which will be deleted during vdev delete.

Existing flag in wdev is used so that driver will be aware of the link
which is going down.

Patch-dependency: 911-a-wifi-mac80211-Add-wdev-specific-flag-to-indicate-NET.patch
		  691-0001-cfg80211-mac80211-add-support-for-channel-switch-wit.patch

Patch-work: none

Signed-off-by: Ramya Gnanasekar <quic_rgnanase@quicinc.com>
